eeks, mostly written, review-bound\" — REFUTED.** 6 of 10 open\n  Windows-titled PRs are CONFLICTING (one is 6509 commits behind), and 5 of 7\n  checked have **never run a single CI check** because they are fork PRs waiting\n  on workflow approval. Rebasing those is authorship, not review.\n- **\"4 of 6 agents emit bash-only hooks\" → 3 of 6.** `factoryaidroid` is\n  Windows-aware on current main. claudecode, geminicli, copilotcli are not.\n- **\"Windows CI guarantees nothing\" — too strong.** It *is* merge-blocking: the\n  required `test` context aggregates and asserts `needs.test-windows.result ==\n  success`. The honest version: **it is a compile-and-link gate wearing a test\n  suite's name.** 21 selected tests, of which only **7** carry Windows-specific\n  signal (the other 14 fake Windows and already run on Linux); the 88-file\n  integration suite and both `main` packages are never compiled on Windows; and\n  golangci-lint never runs with `GOOS=windows`, so `*_windows.go` is unlinted.\n\n## Still true on origin/main (verified today)\n\n- cli `proclive/` has **no `proc_windows.go`** — only `proc_other.go` behind\n  `!linux && !darwin`.\n- cli tree-kill is still a no-op: `execx/execx_windows.go:45` and\n  `procutil/procutil_windows.go:9`, both `func killProcessGroupOnCancel(_ *exec.Cmd) {}`.\n- cli has **no `.gitattributes`**. brain has a good one; graph has none.\n- cli Windows CI is still `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/... -run '(Windows|MSYS)'`.\n- brain has **no `LOCALAPPDATA` anywhere in production code** (only in test\n  isolation tooling).\n- **No long-path handling in any repo**: zero hits for `\\\\?\\`, `core.longpaths`,\n  `MAX_PATH`, `longPathAware`.\n- brain `setup_spawn_windows.go:13` sets `CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP` only.\n\n### The worst Windows bug, and it is data loss\n\ncli's missing `proc_windows.go` makes `OwnerExited()` permanently false on\nWindows, so `finalizeExitedSessions` is a no-op at all four call sites. Two\ncases, and the second is the bad one:\n\n- Agent killed **mid-turn** (ACTIVE): shows normal for 1h (`StuckActiveThreshold`),\n  then \"stale\". Annoying.\n- Agent killed **between turns** (IDLE — the docs say this happens \"just as often\"):\n  `IsStuckActive` gates on `PhaseActive`, so IDLE is **never flagged at all**.\n  After `StaleSessionThreshold` (7 days) `Clear()` deletes the state file,\n  **discarding uncondensed checkpoint work**.\n\nThis is cli, not brain, so it is a review/report item for me — but it should be\nthe top priority in that queue.\n\n## Plan\n\n### Track 0 — code signing (#1505), start today, parallel\n\nProcurement wall-clock dominates (~1-2 weeks); engineering is days. SmartScreen\nblocks ordinary downloads regardless of everything else. Open since 2026-06-23.\nNothing else should queue behind it, and it needs a human to start it.\n\n### Track 1 — build full Windows support in entire-brain (my lane, I write this)\n\nWork against `origin/main` in a fresh worktree, never the stale local checkout.\n**Local branches only — nothing pushed until you say the whole thing is ready.**\nbrain is already actively improving here (Windows skip files dropped 21 → 12,\nnew `brainstore/process_alive_windows.go`, `parentwatch/watch_windows.go`), so\nstep one is re-reading current state rather than trusting the audit.\n\n1. **Store path: add a `LOCALAPPDATA` branch.** `internal/cli/env.go`\n   `resolveXDGDir` (~:121-138) resolves to `%USERPROFILE%\\.local\\share\\...` on\n   Windows while cli hands plugins `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins\\data\\brain`\n   (`plugin_store.go:96-99`). Unix paths agree exactly; only Windows diverges.\n   Also mirror cli's deliberate choice to **ignore `XDG_DATA_HOME` on Windows**\n   (`plugin_store.go:76-79`) — brain honours it on every OS, a second divergence.\n   Scope honestly: the host always sets `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`, so this is a\n   latent correctness bug and a dev footgun, not a user-facing outage. ~5 lines\n   plus a test. Do it because it is cheap and wrong, not because users are hit.\n2. **Detached backfill.** `internal/cli/setup_spawn_windows.go:13` sets only\n   `CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP`. Add `DETACHED_PROCESS | CREATE_NO_WINDOW` so the\n   child neither flashes a console nor dies with the parent console. cli's\n   `execx/execx_windows.go` is the reference implementation.\n3. **`processAlive` hardening.** Re-read `brainstore/process_alive_windows.go`\n   on current main first — it is new since the audit. If it is still\n   `os.FindProcess`-only, add `OpenProcess` + `GetExitCodeProcess` and treat\n   `STILL_ACTIVE` (259) correctly, including the documented ambiguity when a\n   process genuinely exits with 259.\n4. **Long paths: prove, then fix.** Construct an export tree deeper than 260\n   chars (`sessions/branches/<slug80-hash8>/<agent32>/<session80>/<checkpoint32>/…`)\n   and a deep `facts/<slug80>-<hash8>/` path, and assert the write. If it fails,\n   either prefix with `\\\\?\\` at the store writers or document\n   `LongPathsEnabled`. This is absence-of-evidence today — do not budget a fix\n   before the proof.\n5. **CRLF parity test.** Assert identical entities, content hashes and anchors\n   between a CRLF and an LF checkout. None exists. Extend brain's\n   `.gitattributes` if the test finds unpinned byte-exact fixtures.\n6. **OneDrive / network-dir warning in doctor.** `%USERPROFILE%` is commonly\n   OneDrive-redirected and sqlite WAL is unsafe on a synced directory. brain uses\n   WAL (`journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000`). Detect and warn rather than\n   silently corrupt.\n7. **Atomic-replace retry parity.** `internal/config/atomic_replace_windows.go`\n   reportedly lacks the retry-on-`SHARING_VIOLATION` that the `cli`/brainstore\n   variant has. Verify on main, then make them consistent.\n8. **Drain the remaining 12 Windows skip files**, by theme: POSIX permission\n   bits (needs an ACL-based assertion or an explicit documented skip), symlink\n   privilege, POSIX-sh fixtures (port to Go test helpers), unix-domain sockets.\n   Lowest user impact; do it last.\n9. **Windows ARM64 test leg.** brain ships ARM64 artifacts that are never tested.\n\n### Track 2 — review the cli Windows queue (I report; you merge)\n\nI produce a per-PR review note. **I merge and approve nothing.** The ordering\nmatters more than the reviews:\n\n1. **`#2754` or `#3099` must land first.** Both fix `osroot` directory handles\n   blocking `t.TempDir` cleanup on Windows — #2754's own commit reports it was\n   **502 of 542** strategy-package failures on a Windows runner. Every Windows\n   test added by #3070/#3071/#3102 is unreliable until one lands. They are\n   duplicates of each other (`ForgetUnder` vs `ForgetTree`, same three files);\n   **pick one first**, the other needs rewriting.\n2. **Reconcile `#3070` vs `#3102`.** Both close issue #3052, both edit\n   `execx_windows.go` and `procutil_windows.go`. #3070 is the larger unified\n   design (+322 new file, +382 tests, docs); #3102 is a +105 in-place patch.\n   Reviewing both is wasted capacity.\n3. **`#3071`** (proclive on Windows) — the data-loss fix above. Substantial and\n   genuinely test-backed (+265 test lines), but conflicting, never CI'd, and its\n   only real-world validation is an external volunteer who reported a failing\n   test that #2754 fixes. Needs rebase, then CI, then review.\n4. **Close `#1396`** — superseded by main, and worse than what landed.\n5. **Re-scope `#2352`** — half of it landed via #2349 in September; only the BOM\n   half (`skipUTF8BOM`, zero hits on main) is unlanded. It must shed code before\n   review.\n6. **Flag the fork-workflow problem to you.** 5 of 7 checked PRs have never run\n   CI because fork PRs need maintainer workflow approval. Until someone clicks\n   that, \"the engineering is written\" has no verification behind it. This is the\n   cheapest unblock available and only you can do it.\n7. **Add cli's `.gitattributes`**, ported from brain's (targeted rules naming\n   embedded assets and golden fixtures, not a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`).\n   Measured: 0 committed CRLF files in cli and graph, so it breaks nothing today.\n   Report-only; it is cli, not my lane.\n\nContext worth stating plainly: cli has **268 open PRs, 244 `REVIEW_REQUIRED`, 7\napproved**. Review starvation is repo-wide, not a Windows problem.\n\n### Explicitly out of scope\n\n- Widening cli's Windows CI (Track 2 of the earlier draft). That is the \"CI\n  parity\" answer you did not pick, and it is the larger half of the work.\n- graph's POSIX-shell plugin hooks and statusline, and its missing Windows\n  statusline CI leg. Graph's lane, and graph is ~90-95% there.\n- cli code changes of any kind.\n\n## Verification\n\nPer track, and the last point is the honest constraint:\n\n1. **brain store path**: on Windows, `entire-brain.exe status` run directly\n   (no `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`) reports the same store as `entire brain status`.\n   Unit test asserting the Windows branch resolves to `%LOCALAPPDATA%`.\n2. **Detached backfill**: spawn it, close the parent console, confirm the child\n   survives and no console window flashes. Needs a real Windows box.\n3. **Long paths**: the >260-char export-tree test passes, or the\n   `LongPathsEnabled` requirement is documented and doctor checks it.\n4. **CRLF parity**: the new test passes on both a CRLF and an LF checkout in CI.\n5. **No regressions**: brain's Windows CI leg is already a full sharded suite on\n   a required check, so once this is pushed — at the end, on your word — a green\n   `windows-test` is a real signal here, unlike in cli. Until then the strongest\n   local evidence is targeted `GOOS=windows` builds plus the focused tests I can\n   run on macOS, and I will label it as the weaker evidence it is.\n6. **Track 2**: each PR's note names a verdict, blocking issues, and its place in\n   the ordering. Success is you having a merge order, not a merged repo. Nothing\n   is merged, closed or rebased by me.\n7. **Nothing user-facing can be proven from macOS.** Items 2, 3 and 6 need a\n   Windows runner or machine. Where I cannot execute, I will say so rather than\n   claim a bounded source check is equivalent.\n\n## Self-critique — what is still weak\n\n- **Staleness is the standing hazard.** Six agents read stale trees and produced\n  confident wrong findings; I passed two of them to you before catching it. Every\n  step above must re-read `origin/main`.\n- **I have not read the diffs of the cli PRs** this plan proposes ordering.\n  Track 2 step 1's claim that #2754 and #3099 are duplicates comes from a\n  subagent comparing file lists, not from me reading both patches.\n- **brain's current Windows state is better than the audit says** — new\n  `_windows.go` files exist that the audit called missing, skip files dropped\n  21 → 12. Track 1 items 3 and 7 may already be done. Re-read before building.\n- **Items 4, 5 and 6 rest on absence of evidence.** No long-path handling found,\n  no CRLF parity test found, no WAL/OneDrive guard found. Absence of a guard is\n  not proof of a bug; each needs a reproduction first.\n- **No sizing is given on purpose.** My earlier \"2-3 weeks / 4-6 weeks / 2-3\n  months\" came from subagent judgement, not measured throughput, and the\n  review-bound premise underneath it has since been refuted. I would rather give\n  you an estimate after Track 1 item 1 lands and I know what brain's Windows\n  runner actually does with my changes.\n- **No evidence about who the Windows users are.** You said high priority; I have\n  taken that at face value and have not asked what is driving it.\n","isAgent":false,"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/floofy-discovering-bachman.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5f0e0a1-279b-46ce-a91f-84293e233347","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary","grantScope":"session","reasonCode":"unknown"},"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
