{"parentUuid":"4f13039c-c646-47ac-b45a-43edcde363de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwTYDvpSo7Esqy1TFnPL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017oavL9sv3NksJ8qXa7WBKY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/no-merge-asks-until-finished.md <<'MEM_EOF'\n---\nname: no-merge-asks-until-finished\ndescription: \"User (2026-10-24, reaffirmed 2026-11-11) — nothing merges OR PUSHES until ALL the work is finished; stop asking about merges/approvals; handle small decisions myself and keep the todo board free of \\\"waiting on you\\\" noise\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5\n  modified: 2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z\n---\n\nThe user said: *\"I am not merging anything TILL WE FINISH EVERYTHING so stop asking, and on the other stuff you handle it, most is unnecessary and can wait, so clean the slate for me.\"*\n\nReaffirmed 2026-11-11, rejecting a plan approval with: *\"no merging or pushing till we already fully ready\"* — so the rule covers **pushing**, not just merging. This was in response to a plan whose text already said \"I merge and approve nothing\"; that was not explicit enough, because the plan still implied pushing branches to get CI signal.\n\n**Why:** the board had filled with merge/approve/close asks (brain #350, CI approval for fork PRs, #142 rescope), and that read as nagging. The user wants one merge pass at the very end, not a trickle of asks.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- **No `git push`, no `gh pr create`, no merges, approvals, PR closes, rebases of others' PRs, or review comments** until the user says the work is fully ready. Local branches in a worktree only.\n- Do not push merely to obtain CI signal. If a platform runner is the only honest verification, say the claim is unverified rather than pushing to prove it.\n- Recommending an action to the user (for example \"close this superseded PR\") is fine; taking it is not.\n- Make the smaller decisions myself (for example rescoping a PR, or which variant to keep) and note them on the board.\n- On the todo board, `owner: user` is only for things that physically need them, like `/compact`. Everything else is `claude`.\n- Deferred work goes to `todo-board.archive.json` with status `deferred`, not onto the live board.\n\nRelated: [[todo-board-standing-instruction]], [[actually-use-graph-and-brain]].\nMEM_EOF\necho \"memory updated\"\necho\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain\ngit worktree add -b win/full-support /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows origin/main 2>&1 | tail -3\necho\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows 2>/dev/null && echo \"worktree at $(pwd), HEAD=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD), branch=$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)\"","description":"Update memory and create a fresh brain worktree off origin main"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1364,"cache_read_input_tokens":287685,"output_tokens":1248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1364,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1248,"cache_read_input_tokens":287685,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1364},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017oavL9sv3NksJ8qXa7WBKY":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/no-merge-asks-until-finished.md <<'MEM_EOF'\n---\nname: no-merge-asks-until-finished\ndescription: \"User (2026-10-24, reaffirmed 2026-11-11) — nothing merges OR PUSHES until ALL the work is finished; stop asking about merges/approvals; handle small decisions myself and keep the todo board free of \\\"waiting on you\\\" noise\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5\n  modified: 2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z\n---\n\nThe user said: *\"I am not merging anything TILL WE FINISH EVERYTHING so stop asking, and on the other stuff you handle it, most is unnecessary and can wait, so clean the slate for me.\"*\n\nReaffirmed 2026-11-11, rejecting a plan approval with: *\"no merging or pushing till we already fully ready\"* — so the rule covers **pushing**, not just merging. This was in response to a plan whose text already said \"I merge and approve nothing\"; that was not explicit enough, because the plan still implied pushing branches to get CI signal.\n\n**Why:** the board had filled with merge/approve/close asks (brain #350, CI approval for fork PRs, #142 rescope), and that read as nagging. The user wants one merge pass at the very end, not a trickle of asks.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- **No `git push`, no `gh pr create`, no merges, approvals, PR closes, rebases of others' PRs, or review comments** until the user says the work is fully ready. Local branches in a worktree only.\n- Do not push merely to obtain CI signal. If a platform runner is the only honest verification, say the claim is unverified rather than pushing to prove it.\n- Recommending an action to the user (for example \"close this superseded PR\") is fine; taking it is not.\n- Make the smaller decisions myself (for example rescoping a PR, or which variant to keep) and note them on the board.\n- On the todo board, `owner: user` is only for things that physically need them, like `/compact`. Everything else is `claude`.\n- Deferred work goes to `todo-board.archive.json` with status `deferred`, not onto the live board.\n\nRelated: [[todo-board-standing-instruction]], [[actually-use-graph-and-brain]].\nMEM_EOF\necho \"memory updated\"\necho\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain\ngit worktree add -b win/full-support /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows origin/main 2>&1 | tail -3\necho\ncd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows 2>/dev/null && echo \"worktree at $(pwd), HEAD=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD), branch=$(git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)\"","description":"Update memory and create a fresh brain worktree off origin main"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"837147d2-94b0-470e-957b-ec81da6e6dc9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwTYDaiyjrfauHVaAq2f","requestRef":"df83bb59-b0d0-47a4-b1d8-1bc97f8b4100","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"acc0e5b6-cb3f-4bf6-af39-c87f561a7483","timestamp":"2026-11-11T16:30:13.466Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"338a84d2-8297-4418-9431-614af31d9617","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
