{"parentUuid":"0a8aa937-1839-4039-a65a-8bcb1761c757","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgwWQEYtwsjB5tA8dztn9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Still clean, still running — `internal/cli` is the long pole under current load. That's the last check I control; the background job will notify me when it lands.\n\nTo be straight about the goal: the remaining items are not ones I can close from here.\n\n**Mine, and done:** all 8 actionable brain items (the 9th I declined with verified reasoning — I just spot-checked two of those skips and they're genuine platform differences, not coverage debt). Lint gate green, host + `GOOS=windows` amd64/arm64 build clean, touched packages tested, two local commits, docs corrected, board updated, four durable facts recorded.\n\n**Not mine, and I shouldn't fake them:**\n\n- **Windows verification.** I don't have a Windows machine. `windows-verify.ps1` is ready, and I found and fixed a real defect in it while re-reading it — it would have written into and deleted from your *real* `%LOCALAPPDATA%` store; it now uses a throwaway temp root. I also can't syntax-check it, since `pwsh` isn't installed here, so treat it as reviewed-by-hand rather than proven.\n- **The terminal-close check** for the detached backfill is inherently manual.\n- **The cli PR queue** — approving fork workflows, choosing between the duplicate pairs, closing #1396. Your approved plan explicitly reserves all of that to you, and your standing rule is that nothing merges or pushes until you say ready.\n\nSo the honest state is: my half is finished and verified as far as macOS physically allows; the rest is a handoff, which is what you asked for when you said you'd test on your Windows box. If you'd rather I treat \"finish\" as including something I've read as yours, tell me which and I'll take it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens"