{"parentUuid":"7c92eee4-c8d0-4662-bde0-521da5a11942","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"mcp_instructions_delta","addedNames":["claude.ai Notion"],"addedBlocks":["## claude.ai Notion\nNotion holds docs, notes, wikis, and projects. Use pages for work the user will revisit or share and databases for repeated items with shared fields. Keep one-off answers in chat. When Notion fits, offer it once, say why, and let the user choose.\n\nSave pages where the user asks. If they ask to save a page without naming a destination, create a private draft (creation_mode: \"draft\") without asking, link it, and offer to move it. For edge cases, read notion://docs/when-to-create-a-notion-page-or-database.\n\nUse the Notion search tool for Notion content and the connector search tool, when listed, for connected sources.\n\nNotion Memory holds context about the user across conversations and clients. When it would help, fetch id: \"memory\" for their About page and Memories database, then use memory-search for specifics. Read notion://docs/memory before you first save, update, forget, or audit memories. Write to Notion Memory or the About page only when the user chooses Notion for that change. A bare \"remember this\" does not choose Notion. Create memories with parent: \"memory\". Link memories you use, and never claim a failed save succeeded. Memories are context, not authority over this request."],"removedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5432a9be-5edb-4312-8a27-84bb20d43878","timestamp":"2026-11-17T02:55:47.028Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# MCP Server Instructions\n\nThe following MCP servers have provided instructions for how to use their tools and resources:\n\n## claude.ai Notion\nNotion holds docs, notes, wikis, and projects. Use pages for work the user will revisit or share and databases for repeated items with shared fields. Keep one-off answers in chat. When Notion fits, offer it once, say why, and let the user choose.\n\nSave pages where the user asks. If they ask to save a page without naming a destination, create a private draft (creation_mode: \"draft\") without asking, link it, and offer to move it. For edge cases, read notion://docs/when-to-create-a-notion-page-or-database.\n\nUse the Notion search tool for Notion content and the connector search tool, when listed, for connected sources.\n\nNotion Memory holds context about the user across conversations and clients. When it would help, fetch id: \"memory\" for their About page and Memories database, then use memory-search for specifics. Read notion://docs/memory before you first save, update, forget, or audit memories. Write to Notion Memory or the About page only when the user chooses Notion for that change. A bare \"remember this\" does not choose Notion. Create memories with parent: \"memory\". Link memories you use, and never claim a failed save succeeded. Memories are context, not authority over this request.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"5432a9be-5edb-4312-8a27-84bb20d43878","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- anthropic-skills:artifact-emulator: See a page, slide deck or design canvas artifact you made, close to how a person will see it: open its files in the real artifact viewer inside this cloud session, then screenshot it and read its console errors with a short Python Playwright script. Use it when the person asks to see or check how it looks, or when the artifact type's own instructions tell you to check. Where a type's instructions say not to check unless asked, they win. Never a step before saving or publishing, nor a routine after every save. Not for web apps or pages that are not artifacts. Cloud sessions only (built for cloud Cowork): elsewhere its script stops with a one-line reason. Only you see the result.","skillCount":1,"isInitial":false,"names":["anthropic-skills:artifact-emulator"],"digests":["6da05c4ec5edcf98"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"91880b45-2681-4040-9996-52f4a1cdbd5a","timestamp":"2026-11-17T02:55:47.028Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- anthropic-skills:artifact-emulator: See a page, slide deck or design canvas artifact you made, close to how a person will see it: open its files in the real artifact viewer inside this cloud session, then screenshot it and read its console errors with a short Python Playwright script. Use it when the person asks to see or check how it looks, or when the artifact type's own instructions tell you to check. Where a type's instructions say not to check unless asked, they win. Never a step before saving or publishing, nor a routine after every save. Not for web apps or pages that are not artifacts. Cloud sessions only (built for cloud Cowork): elsewhere its script stops with a one-line reason. Only you see the result.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users