{"parentUuid":"fed2e52b-8f69-42b2-9124-fd3025767ced","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_0155cQuf4a8r77eQFfF1xFMW","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows && rtk git log --format='===== %h %s%n%n%b' 8cab9ba6..win/full-support\",\"description\":\"Read the full commit messages\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":20},"type":"attachment","uuid":"77683752-70b4-4f15-8263-282afd1e987e","timestamp":"2026-11-17T02:57:25.007Z","session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"fed2e52b-8f69-42b2-9124-fd3025767ced","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bccffa6e-51d8-4ab5-b9b6-0277a1af5fd4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0155cQuf4a8r77eQFfF1xFMW","type":"tool_result","content":"===== 9512f1b2 docs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narro...\n\nTwo Windows facts the file either omitted or overstated.\n\nThe export tree's relative path is 277 characters worst case, which exceeds\nWin32's 260 before the store root is counted. It works only because Go\nrewrites long absolute paths to the extended \\\\?\\ form, which covers Brain's\nown I/O and nothing else -- git without core.longpaths, backup agents,\nExplorer and user scripts all still see an over-length path. Says so, and\npoints at LongPathsEnabled as the setting that removes the dependency for\nevery tool rather than just this one.\n\nThe path-safety section claimed lock files \"open with O_NOFOLLOW and reject\nsymlinks, hardlinks, and open-file aliasing\". That is true on Unix and only\nhalf true on Windows, where fileLockOpenFlags returns 0: the post-open\nGetFileInformationByHandle check still rejects hardlinks, but the open\nfollows a symlink. Stating one guarantee for both platforms made the weaker\none look like the stronger one.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M75S7HD8BJWK7MADA1RTX6AA\n\n===== 245fa4e2 fix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\n\nSix Windows defects, found by auditing against origin/main rather than the\nlocal checkouts, which were 1007 commits stale.\n\nStore path: the brain resolved its plugin data root through XDG and\n~/.local/share on every OS, while the host CLI ignores XDG on Windows and\nreads %LOCALAPPDATA%. Dispatched runs were fine because the host sets\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR, but a standalone entire-brain.exe read a different,\nempty store and said nothing. Scoped to the data dir only: config, state and\ncache already agree on every OS, and ResolvePluginDirs has 71 callers.\n\nDetached backfill: CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP alone does not detach a child\nfrom the console, so closing the terminal killed the background backfill --\nthe one thing spawnDetached exists to prevent. Adds DETACHED_PROCESS, which\nis safe because stdio already points at a log file. Deliberately not\nCREATE_NO_WINDOW, which Microsoft documents as undefined in combination.\n\nProcessAlive: os.FindProcess succeeds for an exited process whose handle is\nstill open, and os.FindProcess holds exactly such a handle, so a finished\nbackfill reported as running forever and backfillRunning would never start\nanother. Uses WaitForSingleObject, which is unambiguous, rather than\nGetExitCodeProcess, whose STILL_ACTIVE is indistinguishable from a real exit\ncode of 259.\n\nAtomic replace: internal/config made a single MoveFileEx attempt while the\nbrainstore twin retried on sharing and lock violations. The duplication is\nforced by Go's internal-package rule, and is now noted as such.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc5162ce-41b1-41c6-a5dc-5d1a68dfd758","timestamp":"2026-11-17T02:57:25.370Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"===== 9512f1b2 docs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narro...\n\nTwo Windows facts the file either omitted or overstated.\n\nThe export tree's relative path is 277 characters worst case, which exceeds\nWin32's 260 before the store root is counted. It works only because Go\nrewrites long absolute paths to the extended \\\\?\\ form, which covers Brain's\nown I/O and nothing else -- git without core.longpaths, backup agents,\nExplorer and user scripts all still see an over-length path. Says so, and\npoints at LongPathsEnabled as the setting that removes the dependency for\nevery tool rather than just this one.\n\nThe path-safety section claimed lock files \"open with O_NOFOLLOW and reject\nsymlinks, hardlinks, and open-file aliasing\". That is true on Unix and only\nhalf true on Windows, where fileLockOpenFlags returns 0: the post-open\nGetFileInformationByHandle check still rejects hardlinks, but the open\nfollows a symlink. Stating one guarantee for both platforms made the weaker\none look like the stronger one.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M75S7HD8BJWK7MADA1RTX6AA\n\n===== 245fa4e2 fix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\n\nSix Windows defects, found by auditing against origin/main rather than the\nlocal checkouts, which were 1007 commits stale.\n\nStore path: the brain resolved its plugin data root through XDG and\n~/.local/share on every OS, while the host CLI ignores XDG on Windows and\nreads %LOCALAPPDATA%. Dispatched runs were fine because the host sets\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR, but a standalone entire-brain.exe read a different,\nempty store and said nothing. Scoped to the data dir only: config, state and\ncache already agree on every OS, and ResolvePluginDirs has 71 callers.\n\nDetached backfill: CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP alone does not detach a child\nfrom the console, so closing the terminal killed the background backfill --\nthe one thing spawnDetached exists to prevent. Adds DETACHED_PROCESS, which\nis safe because stdio already points at a log file. Deliberately not\nCREATE_NO_WINDOW, which Microsoft documents as undefined in combination.\n\nProcessAlive: os.FindProcess succeeds for an exited process whose handle is\nstill open, and os.FindProcess holds exactly such a handle, so a finished\nbackfill reported as running forever and backfillRunning would never start\nanother. Uses WaitForSingleObject, which is unambiguous, rather than\nGetExitCodeProcess, whose STILL_ACTIVE is indistinguishable from a real exit\ncode of 259.\n\nAtomic replace: internal/config made a single MoveFileEx attempt while the\nbrainstore twin retried on sharing and lock violations. The duplication is\nforced by Go's internal-package rule, and is now noted as such.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7a1c7e46-f01d-4d37-8d22-371ba829baab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":273},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fed2e52b-8f69-42b2-9124-fd3025767ced","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
