{"parentUuid":"e82d477c-8f40-4864-8761-74605939e1fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch7kVqjYox812P5oqV5x2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xa1QMBMLSdnoz43zmcE5PF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit\ncat > \"$KIT/CLAUDE.md\" <<'EOF'\n# You are testing a Windows fix. Read TESTING.md before anything else.\n\nThis repository is a **throwaway verification kit**, not the real project. It is a\nflat export of `entireio/entire-brain` plus two commits that fix six Windows\ndefects. Someone wrote those commits on macOS and **could not execute a single\nuser-facing check**, because every one of them only expresses itself on Windows.\nYou are the execution half of that work.\n\n**Start here: `TESTING.md`.** It is the protocol. `CHANGES.md` says what is under\ntest and, for each item, what the test does and does not prove.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n1. **Do not push, merge, or open a PR anywhere.** Not here, and above all not to\n   `entireio/entire-brain`. This repo has no upstream relationship to it and a\n   push would be wrong in both directions. Commit locally if you must record\n   something; say so in your report.\n2. **Do not fix the code.** If a check fails, that is the finding — the whole\n   point of running it. Report it; do not repair it. A green run you produced by\n   editing the thing under test is worse than a red one.\n3. **Report the actual output.** Paste the real console text, including the lines\n   you do not understand. Do not summarize a failure into a sentence, and do not\n   describe a step you skipped as passed.\n4. **Do not install anything beyond the prerequisites in `TESTING.md`**, and do\n   not change machine settings — in particular do **not** enable the\n   `LongPathsEnabled` registry policy. Section 4 measures whether the code works\n   on a machine in its current state. Changing that setting destroys the\n   measurement.\n5. **Do not run `entire brain` commands against a store you care about.** The\n   script is read-only with respect to the real store; keep it that way.\n\n## If a tool or command is missing\n\nSay so and stop that section. Do not substitute a different command that looks\nequivalent, and do not reason about what the result \"would have been\" — the\nreason this kit exists is that inference from a non-Windows machine already\nfailed once.\nEOF\nwc -l \"$KIT/CLAUDE.md\"","description":"Write CLAUDE.md for the testing agent"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2640,"cache_read_input_tokens":133491,"output_tokens":861,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":861,"cache_read_input_tokens":133491,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12289,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Xa1QMBMLSdnoz43zmcE5PF":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit\ncat > \"$KIT/CLAUDE.md\" <<'EOF'\n# You are testing a Windows fix. Read TESTING.md before anything else.\n\nThis repository is a **throwaway verification kit**, not the real project. It is a\nflat export of `entireio/entire-brain` plus two commits that fix six Windows\ndefects. Someone wrote those commits on macOS and **could not execute a single\nuser-facing check**, because every one of them only expresses itself on Windows.\nYou are the execution half of that work.\n\n**Start here: `TESTING.md`.** It is the protocol. `CHANGES.md` says what is under\ntest and, for each item, what the test does and does not prove.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n1. **Do not push, merge, or open a PR anywhere.** Not here, and above all not to\n   `entireio/entire-brain`. This repo has no upstream relationship to it and a\n   push would be wrong in both directions. Commit locally if you must record\n   something; say so in your report.\n2. **Do not fix the code.** If a check fails, that is the finding — the whole\n   point of running it. Report it; do not repair it. A green run you produced by\n   editing the thing under test is worse than a red one.\n3. **Report the actual output.** Paste the real console text, including the lines\n   you do not understand. Do not summarize a failure into a sentence, and do not\n   describe a step you skipped as passed.\n4. **Do not install anything beyond the prerequisites in `TESTING.md`**, and do\n   not change machine settings — in particular do **not** enable the\n   `LongPathsEnabled` registry policy. Section 4 measures whether the code works\n   on a machine in its current state. Changing that setting destroys the\n   measurement.\n5. **Do not run `entire brain` commands against a store you care about.** The\n   script is read-only with respect to the real store; keep it that way.\n\n## If a tool or command is missing\n\nSay so and stop that section. Do not substitute a different command that looks\nequivalent, and do not reason about what the result \"would have been\" — the\nreason this kit exists is that inference from a non-Windows machine already\nfailed once.\nEOF\nwc -l \"$KIT/CLAUDE.md\"","description":"Write CLAUDE.md for the testing agent"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ab2af5e5-adc3-4d78-81c2-4064d619c7de","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7kVqYdJbGmvYmvhCams","requestRef":"44be000e-b667-46f4-84f3-92e92695c77a","requestedMod