{"parentUuid":"912ccb5f-ba5a-4615-8df4-c21f33a7ab60","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch7kjUVzR83MfdAWf8r3H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Private repo is up:\n\n**https://github.com/suhaanthayyil/entire-brain-windows-verify**\n\nVerified it carries the real thing: the tree at the fix commit is **byte-identical** (`a55b8846`) to `win/full-support`, and the diff matches once git's own index SHAs are excluded.\n\n## What's in it\n\n```\nbaseline  ← untouched export of entireio/entire-brain main @ 8cab9ba6 (tagged)\n  ↓\nfix(windows): make the brain agree with the host on Windows\ndocs(limits): record the Windows path-length ceiling and narrow a lock claim\n  ↓\ntest kit: instructions, verify script, and results template\n```\n\n| File | For |\n|---|---|\n| `CLAUDE.md` | auto-loads in the tester's session — hard rules: don't push, don't fix the code, don't enable `LongPathsEnabled`, report verbatim |\n| `TESTING.md` | the protocol, 275 lines |\n| `CHANGES.md` | all six defects, what each test proves and what it doesn't |\n| `RESULTS-TEMPLATE.md` | the shape the report comes back in |\n| `windows-verify.ps1` | the 5-section script |\n\n12 MB instead of 816 MB — no history, since none of it is needed to build. The `baseline` tag is the load-bearing part: if the suite fails, the tester re-runs that package against untouched upstream, so you get **\"regression\" vs \"pre-existing\"** instead of an ambiguous red.\n\n## Three things I made explicit so you don't get a false green\n\n- **Section 3 will usually only prove the negative half.** Unless that machine's profile is actually OneDrive-redirected, it confirms doctor *doesn't* warn — not that the warning fires. The docs say so and the template has a field for which half ran.\n- **The atomic-replace retry is not verified by this kit.** Nothing here reproduces a `SHARING_VIOLATION`; it needs a second process holding the file open at the instant of replace. Marked \"do not report as verified.\"\n- **The windows/arm64 CI leg is unverifiable here** by design, since nothing pushes.\n\n## Two notes\n\n**Capture is off in the kit** — `.entire/settings.json` set to `enabled: false` and `.claude/settings.json` removed. A throwaway clone with capture on would attribute checkpoints to the wrong repo, which is worse than none. Both are kit-local and flagged as not part of the fix.\n\n**That removal turned up something worth checking.** brain's real `.claude/settings.json` wires every hook as `sh -c '...'`. Git for Windows installs `sh.exe` outside the default PATH, so on a box without Git Bash on PATH those hooks fail at *every* hook event. I haven't confirmed it — I asked the tester to run `Get-Command sh` and report. If it comes back empty, that's a live Windows defect nobody has looked at.\n\nThe repo is under your personal account, so private org code now has a second home — delete it when testing is done. Nothing was pushed to `entireio/entire-brain`; `win/full-support` is still local-only, ahead 2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":149812,"output_tokens":1043,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":637,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":149812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":637},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5fc38f37-548a-486f-84c1-65c8b5e02bac","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch7kjUHM9ybqfJrxMNcCw","requestRef":"d357f4a8