c2344-18a5-4bb8-a811-eb5745247bd4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ee3ee3ac-4bff-466c-8740-58aca097b2b9","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:17:11.096Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"ee3ee3ac-4bff-466c-8740-58aca097b2b9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cd77a49b-0310-4c19-83fd-cbf2eff562e1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GkSp1s6fxSjAJmm5bGBZTz","type":"tool_result","content":"## Headline findings\n\n1. **REGRESSION (defect 1, store path): the fix breaks test-store isolation on Windows.**\n   `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots`, `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks` and `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox` fail on the fix (`bada920` and `HEAD`) and **pass on `baseline`**. Reproduced with the real `%LOCALAPPDATA%` and with it redirected.\n   From reading the code (not fixed): `resolvePluginDataRoot` ignores `XDG_DATA_HOME` on Windows when `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` is unset. But `clitest.PinXDGRoots`, the `TestMain` sandbox for the whole `internal/cli` tree, pins only the four XDG variables. So on Windows every test that resolves the default store now resolves the user's real `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins\\data\\brain`.\n   **Observed consequence:** during section 5, test processes created and populated a real store at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins\\data\\brain\\repos\\local\\stheMiner-2a1c2c75cab9`. `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire` did not exist before the run. It is left in place on purpose; the full listing is in `store-leak-listing.txt`. On `baseline` nothing reached a real store (no `~/.local/share/entire` was created).\n\n2. **DEFECT in defect-4's fix (doctor synced-store warning): the OneDrive warning cannot fire on Windows.**\n   The fix's own new test `TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows` fails 3/3 on Windows: `doctor_synced_store_test.go:44: want a warning, got none`. It is a pure function with an injected environment, so this machine's setup does not affect it.\n   From reading the code: `pathIsUnder` turns `\\` into `/` and then calls `filepath.Clean`. On Windows, `Clean` turns `/` back into `\\`, and the code then checks for a prefix ending in `\"/\"`, which never matches. It passes on macOS because there `Clean` keeps `/`. The UNC branch (`isUNCPath`) does not use `pathIsUnder` and is unaffected.\n   Section 3's PASS is therefore only the trivially true half: doctor can never warn about OneDrive on Windows.\n\n3. **The kit's own commit breaks 5 tests.** `29f0d8e` replaces `README.md`. Because of that, these fail on `HEAD` only and pass on `bada920` and `baseline`:\n   - `TestREADMEDocumentsBothActivationsAndTheirOrder` (agentsetup)\n   - `TestDocContractCapabilityMatrix`\n   - `TestEveryVisibleCommandIsDocumented`\n   - `TestDocumentedCommandContractIsBidirectional`\n   - `TestFeatureMatrixProseMatchesTheData`\n\n   They are not part of the fix. Two related kit mismatches: TESTING.md expects 3 commits but there are 4, and CHANGES.md says `git diff baseline..HEAD` \"is exactly this\", but it also contains the kit commit.\n\n4. **Section 4 measures PowerShell, not the brain.** The probe writes through PowerShell 5.1 / .NET Framework. Its `New-Item -Force` *silently* does not create the 368-char directory: no exception is thrown, and the directory doesn't exist afterwards. `Set-Content` then fails with \"Could not find a part of the path\".\n   A supplementary probe used the same layout but went through Go's `os` package, which is what the exporter uses. It **wrote and read back a 383-char path with `LongPathsEnabled=0`**. So the FAIL confirms docs/limits.md's claim that tools outside Go break on this layout. It is not evidence that Brain's own export fails.\n\n5. **Pre-existing (also on `baseline`): a self-relaunching worker chain under `go test`.** `launchDetachedSelf` re-runs `os.Executable()`, which under test is `cli.test.exe`, as `memory worker --once`. The test binary treats those as positional arguments and runs the whole package again, which reaches the launcher again.\n   During section 5 this built a chain of **34 `cli.test.exe` processes**, each the child of the one before, one new process every 15–75 s. The chain outlived the test run and was still growing when it was killed. It is why `internal/cli` hit the 10-minute timeout. With the chain blocked, the same package finishes in 376 s.\n   On this machine the trigger is that `C:\\Users\\stheMiner` is itself a Git repository (see Environment), so \"not a repository\" temp directories are inside one and code that should exit early reaches the real launcher. Stray `cli.test.exe` processes also appeared after the targeted `baseline` run.\n\n6. **Pre-existing: stock Git for Windows can't check out the repository.** 13 tracked paths exceed 260 characters even at a 48-character clone root. The longest relative path is 215 characters, under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/...`, and `baseline` has the same paths. `git clone` failed with \"Filename too long\" until `core.longpaths=true` was set in the clone's local config. This is the docs/limits.md claim about `git` without `core.longpaths`, confirmed on real hardware, for the project's own repository.\n\n7. **Pre-existing, and the most dangerous: tests write agent setup into the enclosing repository, which here is the user's home folder.** Because `C:\\Users\\stheMiner` is a Git repo, the test suite resolved it as the repo root and wrote:\n   - `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\.entire\\` (created 22:45:45, during the kit's section 5 on `HEAD`)\n   - `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\CLAUDE.md`, `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\AGENTS.md` and `.entire\\agent-guide.md` (23:09:53). That time falls inside the **`baseline`** targeted `internal/cli` run (23:09:20–23:10:05), so this is upstream behaviour, not the fix.\n   - a `PreToolUse` hook merged into `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\.claude\\settings.json` (22:58:53, while the `HEAD` worker chain was running): `cmd /c \"entire-brain hook pre-edit --claude-hook || entire brain hook pre-edit --claude-hook || exit /b 0\"` on `Edit|Write|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit`. **When the repo root is the home folder, `<repo>\\.claude\\settings.json` is the user's global Claude Code settings**, so the hook now runs on every edit in every Claude Code session on this machine. The existing keys were preserved.\n\n   The home repo's `.git` was not modified, and no Git hooks were installed. It's not isolated which test writes these; `TestNestedRepoWarningUsesTheQuotedForm`, which drives a full setup, is the likely one. All of these files are still in place, pending the owner's decision.\n\n## Environment\n=================== ATTRIBUTION ===================\n## Suite failure attribution (TESTING.md section 5)\n\nEach failing test was re-run alone with `-count=1` on `HEAD` (fix + kit), on `bada920` (fix only, before the kit's README swap) and on `baseline`. Raw output is in `attribution-output.txt` and `attribution2-output.txt`.\n\nBecause `internal/cli` timed out, the kit's run never reached every test. So `internal/cli` was also re-run in full with `-timeout 30m` (`cli-full-main.txt`) in a **diagnostic** environment, which is not the kit's environment:\n- `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=C:\\Users\\stheMiner;C:\\Users\\STHEMI~1`, so the home-directory repo isn't discovered and the worker chain doesn't start\n- `LOCALAPPDATA` redirected to `%TEMP%\\brain-lad`, so the regression can't write to the real store\n- `GOCACHE` pinned to its usual location\n\nThat run finished in 376 s with 2,668 PASS, 123 SKIP and 39 FAIL lines (subtests included). No stray processes were left, and 0 files landed under the redirected `LOCALAPPDATA`. It surfaced 23 more failing tests; they were attributed the same way, and the store-path ones were re-run with the real `LOCALAPPDATA` too.\n\n| Package | Test | Fails on fix? | Fails on `baseline`? | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| internal/cli | `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots` | yes (`bada920`, `HEAD`) | **no** (PASS) | **regression** |\n| internal/cli | `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks` | yes | **no** (PASS) | **regression** |\n| internal/cli | `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox` | yes | **no** (PASS) | **regression** |\n| internal/cli | `TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows` | yes | n/a (new in the fix) | **defect in the fix** (new test fails on Windows) |\n| internal/agentsetup | `TestREADMEDocumentsBothActivationsAndTheirOrder` | `HEAD` only; passes on `bada920` | no | kit artifact (README swap) |\n| internal/cli | `TestDocContractCapabilityMatrix`, `TestEveryVisibleCommandIsDocumented`, `TestDocumentedCommandContractIsBidirectional`, `TestFeatureMatrixProseMatchesTheData` | `HEAD` only; pass on `bada920` | no | kit artifact (README swap) |\n| internal/agentsetup | `TestActivationContainedAlias`, `TestActivationDoesNotReadOutsideRepo`, `TestCoordinationLegacyAliasesAndProtectedTargets` | yes | yes | pre-existing: symlink privilege |\n| internal/cli | 29 tests (listed below) | yes | yes | pre-existing: symlink privilege |\n| internal/agentsetup | `TestCoordinationOutsideRepository`, `TestOuterRepoIsEmptyForATopLevelRepo`, `TestOuterRepoRequiresAnInnerRepository` | yes | yes | pre-existing. They report the home directory `C:\\Users\\STHEMI~1` as an outer repo; still fail with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` (the lookup apparently doesn't honour it) |\n| internal/cli | `TestNestedRepoWarningUsesTheQuotedForm`, `TestPlainDirectoryIsNotMistakenForARepository` | yes | yes | pre-existing: home-directory repo. Both pass with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` |\n| tools/coverage | `TestCollectEnvironmentRecordsActualGoConfiguration` | yes | yes | pre-existing: home-directory repo (`WorktreeStatus` reports the home repo). Passes with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` |\n| internal/cli | `TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText`, `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` | yes | yes | pre-existing; cause not determined. The `bare_repository` / `not_a_repository` subtests fail; `no_commits_yet` passes |\n\nThe 29 `internal/cli` symlink-privilege tests, each checked to contain `A required privilege is not held by the client`:\n- `TestBrainBriefGitIntentRejectsSymlinkAndTimeout`\n- `TestPrecedentSourcesDegradeAndDedupe`\n- `TestBrainManifestReaderKeepsFileProtections`\n- `TestHistoryFTSDirectSecurityAndAuthoritativeFailures`\n- `TestAbstractResolverCarriesAffectedJobIssue`\n- `TestAbstractEgressTargetReaderRejectsShardAndLeafSymlinks`\n- `TestAbstractPrivacyCleanupNeverFollowsExternalSymlinks`\n- `TestAbstractReadsFailClosedOnAdversarialArtifacts`\n- `TestPatternCorpusPublishDirectorySwapCannotTouchExternalTarget`\n- `TestFactAvailabilityRejectsEmptyCorruptAndSymlinkStores`\n- `TestWorktreeFingerprintSkipsSymlinksInsideUntrackedDirectory`\n- `TestSemanticChangesDefaultDoesNotAcquireIndexLock`\n- `TestSemanticContextContentSkipsSymlinkedRepoPath`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedLockDirectory`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedBrainRoot`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedBrainParent`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedSnapshotDestination`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkAncestorIntoBrainDir`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkOutputIntoBrainDir`\n- `TestBundleImportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkOutput`\n- `TestWorkspaceRejectsSymlinkedWorkspacePath`\n- `TestWorkspaceCreateIgnoresSymlinkedLegacyTree`\n- `TestSkillFileExistsSeesDanglingSymlink`\n- `TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinkedBase`\n- `TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinkedDestination`\n- `TestPathRefusesSymlinkedStoreRoot`\n- `TestHeadPathForKeyAppliesTheSameGuardsAsBrainDirForKey`\n\nThese tests fail where Windows refuses `os.Symlink` for an unprivileged user, instead of skipping.\n\nFailing output for the regressions and the failing new test:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots (0.00s)\n    main_test.go:44: default plugin directory \"C:\\\\Users\\\\stheMiner\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\entire\\\\plugins\\\\data\\\\brain\" escaped temporary root \"C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\entire-brain-cli-test-xdg-2343469481\": <nil>\n\n--- FAIL: TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks (0.66s)   [HEAD, real LOCALAPPDATA]\n    root_test.go:348: doctor output missing \"plugin data dir: ok (C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks2623373704\\\\001\\\\data\\\\entire\\\\plugins\\\\data\\\\brain\":\n    (doctor instead reports the data dir under %LOCALAPPDATA%; config/state/cache dirs do resolve under the test's XDG root.\n     Full doctor text from the diagnostic run is in cli-full-main.txt)\n\n--- FAIL: TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox (0.00s)   [HEAD, real LOCALAPPDATA]\n    testhome_test.go:115: ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR resolved to \"C:\\\\Users\\\\stheMiner\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\entire\\\\plugins\\\\data\\\\brain\", outside the redirected home \"C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\REDACTED\\\\001\"\n\n--- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows/personal_account (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows/casing_differs_from_the_exported_variable (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows/work_account (0.00s)\n    doctor_synced_store_test.go:44: want a warning, got none   (x3)\n```\n\n## Side observation\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Does `sh` resolve on PATH? (`Get-Command sh`) | **No.** Not before Git was installed, and not after Git for Windows 2.56.0 was installed with default options (only `Git\\cmd` is on PATH). The real repo's `sh -c` hooks would fail on this machine |\n\nAlso seen in passing: setup output says `Watcher unavailable — ... (not supported on windows yet)`.\n\n## Anything you could not do, and why\n\n- **Strong section 1 check and the manual detached-backfill check:** not run, because the host `entire` CLI isn't installed.\n- **Section 3 warning half:** this machine has no OneDrive-redirected profile. The unit test shows the warning can't fire on Windows anyway (Headline 2).\n- **Atomic-replace retry (defect 5):** not verified. Nothing reproduces a `SHARING_VIOLATION`, as the kit says. `internal/config` passed (`ok 1.563s`), so it compiles and doesn't regress.\n- **windows/arm64 CI leg (defect 6):** not verifiable here.\n- **Full-suite `baseline` run:** not done end to end. Attribution was per failing test. The full-package re-run of `internal/cli` was on `HEAD` only, in the diagnostic environment above.\n- **`TestDegenerate*` failures (2):** cause not determined. They are pre-existing.\n\nDeviations from a plain run, all disclosed:\n- **Installs:** Go and Git for Windows were installed with the owner's OK. Both are the kit's listed prerequisites.\n- **Clone:** cloned to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Temp\\brain-win` (short path), with `core.longpaths=true` in the clone's **local** Git config only, which was needed to check out at all (Headline 6). The OS `LongPathsEnabled` policy was not touched.\n- **Cleanup:** the 34 runaway `cli.test.exe` processes were killed after the kit's run finished.\n- **Diagnostic runs:** separate from the kit's run and labelled as such. They used `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`, a redirected `LOCALAPPDATA` and a pinned `GOCACHE`.\n- **Extra probe:** the supplementary Go long-path probe (Headline 4).\n- **Junk store:** left in place at the owner's request (`store-leak-listing.txt`). The kit's rule 5 (\"do not run `entire brain` commands against a store you care about\") was broken by the regression itself, not by any command the kit runs. The machine had no real brain store before this run.\n\nPrivacy note: `verify-output.txt` and `attribution-output.txt` contain, verbatim, the `tools/coverage` test's `git status` listing of the home-directory repository, which names files in the user's home folder. The copy embedded above is redacted.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ab037ba6-3561-4598-beb6-17c27c8cc53f","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:17:11.351Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Headline findings\n\n1. **REGRESSION (defect 1, store path): the fix breaks test-store isolation on Windows.**\n   `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots`, `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks` and `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox` fail on the fix (`bada920` and `HEAD`) and **pass on `baseline`**. Reproduced with the real `%LOCALAPPDATA%` and with it redirected.\n   From reading the code (not fixed): `resolvePluginDataRoot` ignores `XDG_DATA_HOME` on Windows when `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` is unset. But `clitest.PinXDGRoots`, the `TestMain` sandbox for the whole `internal/cli` tree, pins only the four XDG variables. So on Windows every test that resolves the default store now resolves the user's real `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins\\data\\brain`.\n   **Observed consequence:** during section 5, test processes created and populated a real store at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins\\data\\brain\\repos\\local\\stheMiner-2a1c2c75cab9`. `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire` did not exist before the run. It is left in place on purpose; the full listing is in `store-leak-listing.txt`. On `baseline` nothing reached a real store (no `~/.local/share/entire` was created).\n\n2. **DEFECT in defect-4's fix (doctor synced-store warning): the OneDrive warning cannot fire on Windows.**\n   The fix's own new test `TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows` fails 3/3 on Windows: `doctor_synced_store_test.go:44: want a warning, got none`. It is a pure function with an injected environment, so this machine's setup does not affect it.\n   From reading the code: `pathIsUnder` turns `\\` into `/` and then calls `filepath.Clean`. On Windows, `Clean` turns `/` back into `\\`, and the code then checks for a prefix ending in `\"/\"`, which never matches. It passes on macOS because there `Clean` keeps `/`. The UNC branch (`isUNCPath`) does not use `pathIsUnder` and is unaffected.\n   Section 3's PASS is therefore only the trivially true half: doctor can never warn about OneDrive on Windows.\n\n3. **The kit's own commit breaks 5 tests.** `29f0d8e` replaces `README.md`. Because of that, these fail on `HEAD` only and pass on `bada920` and `baseline`:\n   - `TestREADMEDocumentsBothActivationsAndTheirOrder` (agentsetup)\n   - `TestDocContractCapabilityMatrix`\n   - `TestEveryVisibleCommandIsDocumented`\n   - `TestDocumentedCommandContractIsBidirectional`\n   - `TestFeatureMatrixProseMatchesTheData`\n\n   They are not part of the fix. Two related kit mismatches: TESTING.md expects 3 commits but there are 4, and CHANGES.md says `git diff baseline..HEAD` \"is exactly this\", but it also contains the kit commit.\n\n4. **Section 4 measures PowerShell, not the brain.** The probe writes through PowerShell 5.1 / .NET Framework. Its `New-Item -Force` *silently* does not create the 368-char directory: no exception is thrown, and the directory doesn't exist afterwards. `Set-Content` then fails with \"Could not find a part of the path\".\n   A supplementary probe used the same layout but went through Go's `os` package, which is what the exporter uses. It **wrote and read back a 383-char path with `LongPathsEnabled=0`**. So the FAIL confirms docs/limits.md's claim that tools outside Go break on this layout. It is not evidence that Brain's own export fails.\n\n5. **Pre-existing (also on `baseline`): a self-relaunching worker chain under `go test`.** `launchDetachedSelf` re-runs `os.Executable()`, which under test is `cli.test.exe`, as `memory worker --once`. The test binary treats those as positional arguments and runs the whole package again, which reaches the launcher again.\n   During section 5 this built a chain of **34 `cli.test.exe` processes**, each the child of the one before, one new process every 15–75 s. The chain outlived the test run and was still growing when it was killed. It is why `internal/cli` hit the 10-minute timeout. With the chain blocked, the same package finishes in 376 s.\n   On this machine the trigger is that `C:\\Users\\stheMiner` is itself a Git repository (see Environment), so \"not a repository\" temp directories are inside one and code that should exit early reaches the real launcher. Stray `cli.test.exe` processes also appeared after the targeted `baseline` run.\n\n6. **Pre-existing: stock Git for Windows can't check out the repository.** 13 tracked paths exceed 260 characters even at a 48-character clone root. The longest relative path is 215 characters, under `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release/...`, and `baseline` has the same paths. `git clone` failed with \"Filename too long\" until `core.longpaths=true` was set in the clone's local config. This is the docs/limits.md claim about `git` without `core.longpaths`, confirmed on real hardware, for the project's own repository.\n\n7. **Pre-existing, and the most dangerous: tests write agent setup into the enclosing repository, which here is the user's home folder.** Because `C:\\Users\\stheMiner` is a Git repo, the test suite resolved it as the repo root and wrote:\n   - `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\.entire\\` (created 22:45:45, during the kit's section 5 on `HEAD`)\n   - `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\CLAUDE.md`, `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\AGENTS.md` and `.entire\\agent-guide.md` (23:09:53). That time falls inside the **`baseline`** targeted `internal/cli` run (23:09:20–23:10:05), so this is upstream behaviour, not the fix.\n   - a `PreToolUse` hook merged into `C:\\Users\\stheMiner\\.claude\\settings.json` (22:58:53, while the `HEAD` worker chain was running): `cmd /c \"entire-brain hook pre-edit --claude-hook || entire brain hook pre-edit --claude-hook || exit /b 0\"` on `Edit|Write|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit`. **When the repo root is the home folder, `<repo>\\.claude\\settings.json` is the user's global Claude Code settings**, so the hook now runs on every edit in every Claude Code session on this machine. The existing keys were preserved.\n\n   The home repo's `.git` was not modified, and no Git hooks were installed. It's not isolated which test writes these; `TestNestedRepoWarningUsesTheQuotedForm`, which drives a full setup, is the likely one. All of these files are still in place, pending the owner's decision.\n\n## Environment\n=================== ATTRIBUTION ===================\n## Suite failure attribution (TESTING.md section 5)\n\nEach failing test was re-run alone with `-count=1` on `HEAD` (fix + kit), on `bada920` (fix only, before the kit's README swap) and on `baseline`. Raw output is in `attribution-output.txt` and `attribution2-output.txt`.\n\nBecause `internal/cli` timed out, the kit's run never reached every test. So `internal/cli` was also re-run in full with `-timeout 30m` (`cli-full-main.txt`) in a **diagnostic** environment, which is not the kit's environment:\n- `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=C:\\Users\\stheMiner;C:\\Users\\STHEMI~1`, so the home-directory repo isn't discovered and the worker chain doesn't start\n- `LOCALAPPDATA` redirected to `%TEMP%\\brain-lad`, so the regression can't write to the real store\n- `GOCACHE` pinned to its usual location\n\nThat run finished in 376 s with 2,668 PASS, 123 SKIP and 39 FAIL lines (subtests included). No stray processes were left, and 0 files landed under the redirected `LOCALAPPDATA`. It surfaced 23 more failing tests; they were attributed the same way, and the store-path ones were re-run with the real `LOCALAPPDATA` too.\n\n| Package | Test | Fails on fix? | Fails on `baseline`? | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| internal/cli | `TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots` | yes (`bada920`, `HEAD`) | **no** (PASS) | **regression** |\n| internal/cli | `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks` | yes | **no** (PASS) | **regression** |\n| internal/cli | `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox` | yes | **no** (PASS) | **regression** |\n| internal/cli | `TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows` | yes | n/a (new in the fix) | **defect in the fix** (new test fails on Windows) |\n| internal/agentsetup | `TestREADMEDocumentsBothActivationsAndTheirOrder` | `HEAD` only; passes on `bada920` | no | kit artifact (README swap) |\n| internal/cli | `TestDocContractCapabilityMatrix`, `TestEveryVisibleCommandIsDocumented`, `TestDocumentedCommandContractIsBidirectional`, `TestFeatureMatrixProseMatchesTheData` | `HEAD` only; pass on `bada920` | no | kit artifact (README swap) |\n| internal/agentsetup | `TestActivationContainedAlias`, `TestActivationDoesNotReadOutsideRepo`, `TestCoordinationLegacyAliasesAndProtectedTargets` | yes | yes | pre-existing: symlink privilege |\n| internal/cli | 29 tests (listed below) | yes | yes | pre-existing: symlink privilege |\n| internal/agentsetup | `TestCoordinationOutsideRepository`, `TestOuterRepoIsEmptyForATopLevelRepo`, `TestOuterRepoRequiresAnInnerRepository` | yes | yes | pre-existing. They report the home directory `C:\\Users\\STHEMI~1` as an outer repo; still fail with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` (the lookup apparently doesn't honour it) |\n| internal/cli | `TestNestedRepoWarningUsesTheQuotedForm`, `TestPlainDirectoryIsNotMistakenForARepository` | yes | yes | pre-existing: home-directory repo. Both pass with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` |\n| tools/coverage | `TestCollectEnvironmentRecordsActualGoConfiguration` | yes | yes | pre-existing: home-directory repo (`WorktreeStatus` reports the home repo). Passes with `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` |\n| internal/cli | `TestDegenerateRepositoriesAreNamedRatherThanLeakingGitText`, `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` | yes | yes | pre-existing; cause not determined. The `bare_repository` / `not_a_repository` subtests fail; `no_commits_yet` passes |\n\nThe 29 `internal/cli` symlink-privilege tests, each checked to contain `A required privilege is not held by the client`:\n- `TestBrainBriefGitIntentRejectsSymlinkAndTimeout`\n- `TestPrecedentSourcesDegradeAndDedupe`\n- `TestBrainManifestReaderKeepsFileProtections`\n- `TestHistoryFTSDirectSecurityAndAuthoritativeFailures`\n- `TestAbstractResolverCarriesAffectedJobIssue`\n- `TestAbstractEgressTargetReaderRejectsShardAndLeafSymlinks`\n- `TestAbstractPrivacyCleanupNeverFollowsExternalSymlinks`\n- `TestAbstractReadsFailClosedOnAdversarialArtifacts`\n- `TestPatternCorpusPublishDirectorySwapCannotTouchExternalTarget`\n- `TestFactAvailabilityRejectsEmptyCorruptAndSymlinkStores`\n- `TestWorktreeFingerprintSkipsSymlinksInsideUntrackedDirectory`\n- `TestSemanticChangesDefaultDoesNotAcquireIndexLock`\n- `TestSemanticContextContentSkipsSymlinkedRepoPath`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedLockDirectory`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedBrainRoot`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedBrainParent`\n- `TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedSnapshotDestination`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkAncestorIntoBrainDir`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkOutputIntoBrainDir`\n- `TestBundleImportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog`\n- `TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkOutput`\n- `TestWorkspaceRejectsSymlinkedWorkspacePath`\n- `TestWorkspaceCreateIgnoresSymlinkedLegacyTree`\n- `TestSkillFileExistsSeesDanglingSymlink`\n- `TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinkedBase`\n- `TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinkedDestination`\n- `TestPathRefusesSymlinkedStoreRoot`\n- `TestHeadPathForKeyAppliesTheSameGuardsAsBrainDirForKey`\n\nThese tests fail where Windows refuses `os.Symlink` for an unprivileged user, instead of skipping.\n\nFailing output for the regressions and the failing new test:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestTestMainPinsXDGRoots (0.00s)\n    main_test.go:44: default plugin directory \"C:\\\\Users\\\\stheMiner\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\entire\\\\plugins\\\\data\\\\brain\" escaped temporary root \"C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\entire-brain-cli-test-xdg-2343469481\": <nil>\n\n--- FAIL: TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks (0.66s)   [HEAD, real LOCALAPPDATA]\n    root_test.go:348: doctor output missing \"plugin data dir: ok (C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks2623373704\\\\001\\\\data\\\\entire\\\\plugins\\\\data\\\\brain\":\n    (doctor instead reports the data dir under %LOCALAPPDATA%; config/state/cache dirs do resolve under the test's XDG root.\n     Full doctor text from the diagnostic run is in cli-full-main.txt)\n\n--- FAIL: TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox (0.00s)   [HEAD, real LOCALAPPDATA]\n    testhome_test.go:115: ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR resolved to \"C:\\\\Users\\\\stheMiner\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\entire\\\\plugins\\\\data\\\\brain\", outside the redirected home \"C:\\\\Users\\\\STHEMI~1\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\REDACTED\\\\001\"\n\n--- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows/personal_account (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows/casing_differs_from_the_exported_variable (0.00s)\n    --- FAIL: TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows/work_account (0.00s)\n    doctor_synced_store_test.go:44: want a warning, got none   (x3)\n```\n\n## Side observation\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Does `sh` resolve on PATH? (`Get-Command sh`) | **No.** Not before Git was installed, and not after Git for Windows 2.56.0 was installed with default options (only `Git\\cmd` is on PATH). The real repo's `sh -c` hooks would fail on this machine |\n\nAlso seen in passing: setup output says `Watcher unavailable — ... (not supported on windows yet)`.\n\n## Anything you could not do, and why\n\n- **Strong section 1 check and the manual detached-backfill check:** not run, because the host `entire` CLI isn't installed.\n- **Section 3 warning half:** this machine has no OneDrive-redirected profile. The unit test shows the warning can't fire on Windows anyway (Headline 2).\n- **Atomic-replace retry (defect 5):** not verified. Nothing reproduces a `SHARING_VIOLATION`, as the kit says. `internal/config` passed (`ok 1.563s`), so it compiles and doesn't regress.\n- **windows/arm64 CI leg (defect 6):** not verifiable here.\n- **Full-suite `baseline` run:** not done end to end. Attribution was per failing test. The full-package re-run of `internal/cli` was on `HEAD` only, in the diagnostic environment above.\n- **`TestDegenerate*` failures (2):** cause not determined. They are pre-existing.\n\nDeviations from a plain run, all disclosed:\n- **Installs:** Go and Git for Windows were installed with the owner's OK. Both are the kit's listed prerequisites.\n- **Clone:** cloned to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Temp\\brain-win` (short path), with `core.longpaths=true` in the clone's **local** Git config only, which was needed to check out at all (Headline 6). The OS `LongPathsEnabled` policy was not touched.\n- **Cleanup:** the 34 runaway `cli.test.exe` processes were killed after the kit's run finished.\n- **Diagnostic runs:** separate from the kit's run and labelled as such. They used `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`, a redirected `LOCALAPPDATA` and a pinned `GOCACHE`.\n- **Extra probe:** the supplementary Go long-path probe (Headline 4).\n- **Junk store:** left in place at the owner's request (`store-leak-listing.txt`). The kit's rule 5 (\"do not run `entire brain` commands against a store you care about\") was broken by the regression itself, not by any command the kit runs. The machine had no real brain store before this run.\n\nPrivacy note: `verify-output.txt` and `attribution-output.txt` contain, verbatim, the `tools/coverage` test's `git status` listing of the home-directory repository, which names files in the user's home folder. The copy embedded above is redacted.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"31278572-3f96-43e2-881d-3f96bfb3c567","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","branch":"win/full-support","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee3ee3ac-4bff-466c-8740-58aca097b2b9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015-41c2-a29f-4f2db2f6e0cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
