{"parentUuid":"84dbdeb4-66ef-4b03-9df6-3941c4780dee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9Cv8YGw88Jm2RX3y4kd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TREAxARFmtnqxE8uHGokPS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Convert symlink test sites to skip","model":"sonnet","prompt":"Work in the git worktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows (branch win/full-support). Do NOT cd elsewhere, do NOT commit, do NOT push, do NOT touch any other repo.\n\nGOAL\nOn Windows, an unprivileged account without Developer Mode gets \"A required privilege is not held by the client\" from os.Symlink. 32 tests FAIL on that instead of SKIPPING. Make them skip.\n\nHELPERS ALREADY EXIST — do not write new ones:\n- package cli: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/internal/cli/symlink_test.go provides\n    skipIfSymlinksUnrepresentable(t *testing.T)\n    symlinkForTest(t *testing.T, target, link string)\n- package agentsetup: internal/agentsetup/agents_test.go already provides\n    skipIfSymlinksUnrepresentable(t *testing.T)   (around line 579)\n    symlinkForTest(t *testing.T, target, link string)   (around line 1719)\n  NOTE: agentsetup's symlinkForTest currently does `t.Fatal(err)`. Change ONLY that one function body to skip on a privilege error the way package cli's version does (match the cli implementation's behaviour; agentsetup may need the same errors/syscall imports).\n\nCONVERSION RULE\nFor each named test below, find the os.Symlink call(s) it actually reaches, including ones inside local helper closures or table-driven `mutate`/`setup` funcs:\n1. If the shape is `if err := os.Symlink(a, b); err != nil { t.Fatal/t.Fatalf(...) }` -> replace the whole block with `symlinkForTest(t, a, b)`.\n2. If the symlink is created somewhere that has no *testing.T in scope, instead add `skipIfSymlinksUnrepresentable(t)` as the first statement of the narrowest enclosing scope that does have `t` — the subtest if only a subtest symlinks, otherwise the test function.\n3. DO NOT convert a call whose error is asserted on (a test that EXPECTS os.Symlink to fail, or stores the error for comparison). Leave it and report it.\n4. DO NOT change any assertion, fixture content, test name or non-test file.\n5. Some sites already have `if runtime.GOOS == \"windows\" { t.Skip(...) }`. Replace that blanket skip with the probe/helper so Developer Mode and CI still get coverage. If removing it leaves `runtime` unused, drop the import.\n\nTESTS IN package cli (files: /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows/internal/cli/*_test.go, NOT subdirectories):\nTestBrainBriefGitIntentRejectsSymlinkAndTimeout, TestPrecedentSourcesDegradeAndDedupe, TestBrainManifestReaderKeepsFileProtections, TestHistoryFTSDirectSecurityAndAuthoritativeFailures, TestAbstractResolverCarriesAffectedJobIssue, TestAbstractEgressTargetReaderRejectsShardAndLeafSymlinks, TestAbstractPrivacyCleanupNeverFollowsExternalSymlinks, TestAbstractReadsFailClosedOnAdversarialArtifacts, TestPatternCorpusPublishDirectorySwapCannotTouchExternalTarget, TestFactAvailabilityRejectsEmptyCorruptAndSymlinkStores, TestWorktreeFingerprintSkipsSymlinksInsideUntrackedDirectory, TestSemanticChangesDefaultDoesNotAcquireIndexLock, TestSemanticContextContentSkipsSymlinkedRepoPath, TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedLockDirectory, TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedBrainRoot, TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedBrainParent, TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinkedSnapshotDestination, TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog, TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkAncestorIntoBrainDir, TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkOutputIntoBrainDir, TestBundleImportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog, TestBundleExportRejectsSymlinkOutput, TestWorkspaceRejectsSymlinkedWorkspacePath, TestWorkspaceCreateIgnoresSymlinkedLegacyTree, TestSkillFileExistsSeesDanglingSymlink, TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinkedBase, TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinkedDestination, TestPathRefusesSymlinkedStoreRoot, TestHeadPathForKeyAppliesTheSameGuardsAsBrainDirForKey\n\nTESTS IN package agentsetup (internal/agentsetup/*_test.go):\nTestActivationContainedAlias, TestActivationDoesNotReadOutsideRepo, TestCoordinationLegacyAliasesAndProtectedTargets\n\nVERIFY BEFORE REPORTING (run each; do not chain through `head`/`tail` in a way that hides a non-zero exit):\n  cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-windows\n  gofmt -l internal/cli internal/agentsetup          # must print nothing\n  go build ./...                                      # must exit 0\n  go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/agentsetup         # must exit 0\n  GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./internal/agentsetup -count=1\n  GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./internal/cli -count=1 -run 'TestBrainBriefGitIntentRejectsSymlinkAndTimeout|TestPrecedentSourcesDegradeAndDedupe|TestBrainManifestReaderKeepsFileProtections|TestHistoryFTSDirectSecurityAndAuthoritativeFailures|TestAbstractResolverCarriesAffectedJobIssue|TestAbstractEgressTargetReaderRejectsShardAndLeafSymlinks|TestAbstractPrivacyCleanupNeverFollowsExternalSymlinks|TestAbstractReadsFailClosedOnAdversarialArtifacts|TestPatternCorpusPublishDirectorySwapCannotTouchExternalTarget|TestFactAvailabilityRejectsEmptyCorruptAndSymlinkStores|TestWorktreeFingerprintSkipsSymlinksInsideUntrackedDirectory|TestSemanticChangesDefaultDoesNotAcquireIndexLock|TestSemanticContextContentSkipsSymlinkedRepoPath|TestSemanticIndexRejectsSymlinked|TestBundleExportRejectsSymlink|TestBundleImportRejectsSymlinkedAuditLog|TestWorkspaceRejectsSymlinkedWorkspacePath|TestWorkspaceCreateIgnoresSymlinkedLegacyTree|TestSkillFileExistsSeesDanglingSymlink|TestSkillWriteRefusesSymlinked|TestPathRefusesSymlinkedStoreRoot|TestHeadPathForKeyAppliesTheSameGuardsAsBrainDirForKey'\nAll must pass on macOS (symlinks DO work here, so these run for real — they must still PASS, not skip; a skip on macOS means you broke something).\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n- Do not run the full ./... test suite (CPU contention with other sessions). Only the targeted runs above.\n- Use rtk for git/shell where available.\n- 