scape | `TestDoctorUsesXDGFallbacks` | |\n| F1 sandbox escape | `TestDefaultStoreFallbackStaysInsideTheSandbox` | |\n| F1 real-world effect | did `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire` grow during the run? | |\n| F2 OneDrive comparison | `TestSyncedStoreDirDetailFlagsOneDriveOnWindows` | |\n| P2 worker chain | stray `cli.test.exe` count after section 6 | |\n| P2 worker chain | did `internal/cli` finish without timing out? | |\n| P3 symlink tests | how many **skipped** (should be ~32, previously failures)? | |\n| P1 home writes | anything new in `%USERPROFILE%` during this run? | |\n\n## Manual check — detached backfill (TESTING.md §5)\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Ran `entire brain setup`? | |\n| Closed the terminal window (X, not Ctrl-C)? | |\n| Did `entire-brain.exe` survive? | |\n| Did a console window flash when it started? | |\n| If not run, why | |\n\n## Suite failure attribution (TESTING.md §6)\n\n| Package | Test | Fails on `fix-tip`? | Fails on `baseline`? | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | | pre-existing / **regression** |\n\n```\n<paste failing output>\n```\n\n## Known-open\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `TestDegenerate*` / `TestWorktreeRefreshNamesADegenerateRepository` still failing? | |\n| Any insight into why? (bonus, not expected) | |\n\n## Anything you could not do, and why\n\n<free text — as valuable as the passes>\n\n## Anything the kit itself got wrong\n\n<round 1 found five of these; please keep looking>\nEOF\n# Capture hooks off: a throwaway clone must not attribute checkpoints anywhere.\nrm -f \"$KIT/.claude/settings.json\"\npython3 - <<PY\nimport json, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"$KIT/.entire/settings.json\")\nd = json.loads(p.read_text()); d[\"enabled\"]=False; d[\"telemetry\"]=False\np.write_text(json.dumps(d, indent=2)+\"\\n\")\nPY\necho \"=== README.md untouched? (K1) ===\"\ncd \"$KIT\" && git status --short README.md && echo \"  (no output above = untouched)\"\ngit status --short | head -20","description":"Write the results template and disable capture"},"c