{"parentUuid":"be3107cb-e55f-4180-9d79-3436ea5d0ca1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ch9EDCwnSKTP5CrpyhzEb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BM47524aSnMLCj4yHx3Z6e","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncd \"$KIT\"\ngit add -A\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest kit: round 2 — protocol, Go long-path probe, results template\n\nAdds what an independent tester needs to confirm the six fixes made after\nthe first Windows run, plus the checks round 1 could not reach.\n\nFixes the five faults that run found in the kit itself:\n- the project README.md is left untouched. Replacing it broke five\n  documentation-contract tests, which then looked like product failures.\n  The kit's own overview lives in VERIFY-KIT.md.\n- baseline and fix-tip tags bound the change, so the diff range is exact\n  and does not drift when the kit gains commits.\n- section 4 probes long paths through Go, not PowerShell. PowerShell\n  5.1's New-Item -Force silently fails at ~368 characters, so the old\n  probe measured PowerShell rather than the exporter and reported a FAIL\n  for behaviour that works.\n- section 6 sets GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES and section 7 counts stray test\n  binaries, which is how the 34-process chain went unnoticed until it had\n  timed the suite out.\n- preflight detects a git repository enclosing the home or temp directory\n  and says so, because it changes many results.\n\nSection 7 also snapshots the real store before the run and compares after,\nso the sandbox escape cannot come back unnoticed.\n\nKit-local and NOT part of the fix: capture hooks disabled\n(.entire/settings.json enabled:false, .claude/settings.json removed) so a\nthrowaway clone cannot attribute checkpoints to the wrong repository, and\nCLAUDE.md replaced to point at the protocol. Originals are in baseline.\nEOF\ngit tag -f fix-tip $(git rev-parse HEAD~1) >/dev/null\necho \"=== log ===\"; git log --oneline | head -3\necho \"=== tags ===\"; git tag -l | sed 's/^/  /'\necho \"=== diff baseline..fix-tip stat (must be the product change only) ===\"\ngit diff --stat baseline..fix-tip | tail -3\necho \"=== diff fix-tip..HEAD (kit files only) ===\"\ngit diff --name-only fix-tip..HEAD | sed 's/^/  /'","description":"Commit the kit and set the fix-tip tag"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2022,"cache_read_input_tokens":309505,"output_tokens":1382,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":393},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2022,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":309505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2022},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":12312,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BM47524aSnMLCj4yHx3Z6e":{"command":"set -e\nKIT=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad/winkit2\ncd \"$KIT\"\ngit add -A\ngit -c user.name=\"Suhaan Thayyil\" commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest kit: round 2 — protocol, Go long-path probe, results template\n\nAdds what an independent tester needs to confirm the six fixes made after\nthe first Windows run, plus the checks round 1 could not reach.\n\nFixes the five faults that run found in the kit itself:\n- the project README.md is left untouched. Replacing it broke five\n  documentation-contract tests, which then looked like product failures.\n  The kit's own overview lives in VERIFY-KIT.md.\n- baseline and fix-tip tags bound the change, so the diff range is exact\n  and does not drift when the kit gains commits.\n- section 4 probes long paths through Go, not PowerShell. PowerShell\n  5.1's New-Item -Force silently fails at ~368 characters, so the old\n  probe measured PowerShell rather than the exporter and reported a FAIL\n  for behaviour that works.\n- section 6 sets GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES and section 7 counts stray test\n  binaries, which is how the 34-process chain went unnoticed until it had\n  timed the suite out.\n- preflight detects a git repository enclosing the home or temp directory\n  and says so, because it changes many results.\n\nSection 7 also snapshots the real store before the run and compares after,\nso the sandbox escape cannot come back unnoticed.\n\nKit-local and NOT part of the fix: capture hooks disabled\n(.entire/settings.json enabled:false, .claude/settings.json removed) so a\nthrowaway clone cannot attribute checkpoints to the wrong repository, and\nCLAUDE.md replaced to point at the protocol. Originals are in baseline.\nEOF\ngit tag -f fix-tip $(git rev-parse HEAD~1) >/dev/null\necho \"=== log ===\"; git log --oneline | head -3\necho \"=== tags ===\"; git tag -l | sed 's/^/  /'\necho \"=== diff baseline..fix-tip stat (must be the product change only) ===\"\ngit diff --stat baseline..fix-tip | tail -3\necho \"=== diff fix-tip..HEAD (kit files only) ===\"\ngit diff --name-only fix-tip..HEAD | sed 's/^/  /'","description":"Commit the kit and set the fix-tip tag"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bec2af82-c903-4f05-846c-5b4605718052","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Ch9EDCNZ1cC2Uqx8wSQGh","requestRef":"24881967-258d-472d-8a62-d4a350ee09c5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"9dc526eb-cb1a-4bbe-a05c-f7f971eba4f2","timestamp":"2026-11-17T21:42:39.255Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"1041b1a0-c015